r#  87260  1638  69
p: .
t. 
|  Such <!!"!!>roles<!!"!!> may be outside the normal
|  scope of lambda calculi (or other computation-models), but there are
|  related ideas in
.  hypergraph databases, or similar knowledge-representation techniques


--- Sentence/switch
id: 482
r#  87261  1638  70


--- Sentence//end
id: 482
r#  87510  1642  48
p: .
t. 
|  A multi-part relation (schematically a hyperedge) can assign distinct roles
|  to each participant; e.g., divorce implies two individuals,
|  a prior situation of marriage, and some legal entity or
.  context which recognizes the divorce as binding


--- Sentence/switch
id: 483
r#  87511  1642  49


--- Sentence//end
id: 483
r#  87714  1646  9
p: .
t. 
|  A binary relation such that one party is divorced from
|  another thereby implies the presence of further participants
|  (so treating this relation as merely arity-two excludes constitutive
.  details)

--- Sentence/end 
