.   @l() -89154/1673/34
p: .
t. 
|  Conceptual integration is in some sense an
|  intellectual procedure -=- <!!"!!>computing<!!"!!> in the
|  domain of conceptual staging and proto-images, if we don't take the mind/machine
|  metaphor too literally -=- and
|  language-users deploy background knowledge
.  to <!!"!!>execute<!!"!!> such scripts in comunally-sanctioned ways

